# The walker against the REAL server (piece 2; turns are piece 3 and not on it yet). Run it with
# scripts/real-server-check.sh, which pairs, plants configuration 2, and drives what a script can't: it
# pauses and resumes the server and forgets the walker while steps 4-6 wait.

# 1. Boot and reach the real server. The runner planted configuration 2 "from an earlier pairing", so the
#    heartbeat's version 1 differs and the walker fetches configuration 1 from the server.
expect spoke Steady is on.
expect link online
expect heartbeat ok
expect config 1

# 2. Configuration 1 (vibration) is in force: an obstacle buzzes the simulated handle.
key n
expect haptic near_obstacle
key f
wait 300

# 3. A Talk turn: the server has no turns route yet, so the walker says its fixed server-trouble line.
key t
expect talk recording
wait 1200
key t
expect turn failed
expect spoke Something went wrong on the server.
# Confirm with nothing open: the short sound, no request.
key c
expect cue nothing_to_confirm

# 4. The runner pauses the dev server (SIGSTOP): its requests hang, so the walker goes offline within
#    two heartbeats. Obstacle cues keep working.
expect 60000 link offline
expect spoke I'm offline right now. Your vibration alerts still work.
key n
expect haptic near_obstacle
key f

# 5. The runner resumes it (SIGCONT): the next heartbeat gets through and the walker says so.
expect 60000 link online
expect spoke I'm back online.

# 6. The runner forgets the walker on the server (DELETE /api/v1/walkers/{id}): 401, "pair me again".
expect 60000 link unauthorized
expect spoke I need to be paired again.
key t
expect spoke I need to be paired again.
key q
